+**Ending**: how a run finished, written when it happens — accepted, turned down, refused to the end, done, fallen over, or stopped. *Done* is a run with nothing to accept or turn down, which is what reading a report is. *Stopped* is a run the user ended without answering it: replaced by a correction or a new ask, mid-plan or while its proposal waited, with the replacing run following it in the same negotiation; or an adaptation whose workout they then reported. A run that is waiting on an answer has no ending, and neither has one that was cut.
 
